{"id":15598,"date":"2026-07-09T07:55:42","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T07:55:42","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/?p=15598"},"modified":"2026-07-28T11:55:01","modified_gmt":"2026-07-28T11:55:01","slug":"youtube-income-per-1000-views","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/youtube-income-per-1000-views\/","title":{"rendered":"YouTube Income Per 1000 Views &amp; 10000 Views in India (2026)"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Have you ever watched a YouTube video with millions of views and wondered, &#8220;How much money did the creator actually make?&#8221; It&#8217;s one of the most common questions among aspiring YouTubers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The truth is, YouTube does not pay a fixed amount for every 1,000 views. Two creators can get the same number of views but earn completely different amounts. Your earnings depend on several factors, including your content niche, audience location, video length, watch time, ad types, and overall engagement.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In India, the average YouTube income per 1000 views usually ranges from \u20b950 to \u20b9200 for many channels. However, creators in high-paying niches such as finance, business, software, and technology can earn \u20b9500, \u20b91,000, or even more per 1,000 monetized views because advertisers are willing to pay higher rates.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>At <strong>WsCube Tech<\/strong>, we&#8217;ve experienced this firsthand. Over the last five years, our YouTube channel has grown to 4+ million subscribers, helping millions of learners build skills in digital marketing, programming, data science, and more. Through this journey, we&#8217;ve gained practical insights into YouTube monetization, CPM, RPM, ad revenue, and the factors that influence creator earnings. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>By the end of this guide, you\u2019ll know:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>How YouTube pays creators<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>What CPM, RPM, and monetized views mean<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How much you can realistically earn per 1000 views in India<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>The difference between Shorts and long videos<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>How to increase your YouTube earnings<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Whether you&#8217;re planning to start a YouTube channel or want to earn more from your existing videos, this guide will help you understand YouTube monetization in simple words.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>If you want to grow your YouTube Income, learning the right strategy is important. Just our <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/digital-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">best online digital marketing course<\/a> to understand monetization, growth and hashtags. You&#8217;ll also learn <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/360-digital-marketing\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">360\u00b0 digital marketing<\/a>, including <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO<\/a>, social media and paid ads to scale your channel faster.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Average YouTube Income Per 1000 Views in India<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Based on current ad rates and real-world data, YouTube income per 1000 views in India falls between \u20b950 to \u20b9200.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>View Count<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Estimated Earnings (\u20b9)<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1,000 views<\/td><td>\u20b950 \u2013 \u20b9200<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>10,000 views<\/td><td>\u20b9500 \u2013 \u20b92,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>100,000 (1 lakh) views<\/td><td>\u20b95,000 \u2013 \u20b920,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1,000,000 (10 lakh) views<\/td><td>\u20b950,000 \u2013 \u20b92,00,000<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The variation depends on your video\u2019s topic, audience, and ad type.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>For example, a finance video targeti