rong>Requirement<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Description<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>1,000 Subscribers<\/td><td>Must have at least 1,000 active subscribers.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>4,000 Watch Hours (or 10M Shorts views)<\/td><td>Required within the last 12 months.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Linked AdSense Account<\/td><td>Needed to receive payments.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>No Community Strikes<\/td><td>You must follow YouTube\u2019s community and copyright policies.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Original, High-Quality Content<\/td><td>Reused or repetitive content is not allowed under new rules.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Once you meet these conditions, you can apply for monetization from your YouTube Studio dashboard.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-make-money-digital-marketing\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Make Money in Digital Marketing? 12 Best Ways<\/a>&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How YouTube Monetization Works?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Advertisers Pay YouTube to Show Ads<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Brands pay YouTube to display their ads on relevant videos. The ad rates vary depending on niche, audience type, and overall competition among advertisers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. YouTube Places Ads on Eligible Videos<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Once your channel joins the YouTube Partner Program, ads appear on your videos based on viewer location, language, and advertiser preferences.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Ads Generate Revenue When Viewed or Clicked<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>You earn money only when viewers actually see or interact with ads\u2014either by watching for a few seconds or clicking through.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. YouTube Splits the Ad Revenue with You<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>YouTube keeps around 45% of the total ad revenue and gives creators 55%. This is calculated automatically through Google AdSense.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Payments Are Released via Google AdSense<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Your income accumulates monthly, and once it crosses \u20b97,000 (or $100), YouTube transfers the amount directly to your linked AdSense bank account.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Key Terms You Must Know<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. CPM (Cost Per Mille)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>It is the amount advertisers pay YouTube for 1,000 ad impressions.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>High CPM = high advertiser demand.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. RPM (Revenue Per Mille)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>It is your actual earnings per 1,000 views after YouTube\u2019s cut. It includes revenue from ads, memberships, Super Chats, etc.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Formula:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>RPM <\/strong>= (Total Revenue \u00f7 Total Views) \u00d7 1000<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. CTR (Click-Through Rate)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>It is the percentage of people who click on your video after seeing it in their feed. A higher CTR usually improves earnings.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4. Watch Time<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Total minutes viewers spend on your video. More watch time means better ad placement and higher CPM.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">5. Monetized Views<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Not every view shows an ad. Usually, 40%\u201380% of your total views are monetized depending on audience location and ad availability.<\/p>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n                <p>Attend our live classes led by experienced and desiccated instructors of Wscube Tech.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel myOwl\">\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cracking-meta-google-ads-2026-data-automation-attribution?utm_sou