ooming-digital-marketing-career-in-ai-era?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-07T104930_382_1786105407836_186872.webp\" alt=\"Booming Digital Marketing Career in AI Era\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cybersecurity-professional-career-roadmap-2026-2?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-05T122121_005_1786351858212_930412.webp\" alt=\"Cybersecurity Professional Career Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">High-Earning Niches on YouTube<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Some niches pay higher CPMs because advertisers in those fields spend more to reach specific audiences.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Top-Earning Niches<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Why They Have Higher CPM?<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Finance &amp; Investing<\/td><td>Banks and fintech brands pay more to reach people looking for money tips or investments.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Tech &amp; Gadgets<\/td><td>Big tech brands spend heavily on phone, laptop, and software ads.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Education &amp; Career<\/td><td>Edtech companies and job portals target students and professionals.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Business &amp; Startups<\/td><td>Serious audiences attract high-value brand ads.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Software &amp; SaaS Reviews<\/td><td>Brands pay well for niche, review-based content.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Factors That Affect YouTube Earnings Per 1000 Views<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1654\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/factors-that-affect-youtube-earnings.webp\" alt=\"Factors That Affect YouTube Earnings Per 1000 Views\" class=\"wp-image-20392\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/factors-that-affect-youtube-earnings.webp 1654w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/factors-that-affect-youtube-earnings-300x181.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/factors-that-affect-youtube-earnings-1024x619.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/factors-that-affect-youtube-earnings-768x464.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/04\/factors-that-affect-youtube-earnings-1536x929.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1654px) 100vw, 1654px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Your earnings depend on many things, and understanding them helps you optimize your channel.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>1. Audience Location: <\/strong>Views from countries like the US, UK, and Canada bring higher CPM than Indian views.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>2. Video Niche: <\/strong>Finance, tech, and education content earn more than vlogs, entertainment, or music.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>3. Ad Type: <\/strong>Skippable video ads pay less than display or bumper ads.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>4. Viewer Engagement: <\/strong>Higher watch time, likes, and comments tell YouTube your video has value \u2014 improving ad rates.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>5. Content Length: <\/strong>Videos longer than 8 minutes allow mid-roll ads, increasing total revenue.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>6. Device Type: <\/strong>Desktop viewers see more ads than mobile users, especially in India where many people use ad blockers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>7. Time of Year:<\/strong> Festive months like November\u2013December see higher CPMs as brands spend more.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Suggested Reading:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-make-money-with-ai\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Make Money With AI? 10 Ways<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">YouTube Income for Shorts vs Long Videos<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>YouTube Shorts are great for reach, but not so great for revenue. Below is a simple comparison:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Video Type<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Average RPM in India<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Example (1M Views)<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Shorts<\/td><td>\u20b95 \u2013 \u20b930<\/td><td>\u20b95,000 \u2013 \u20b930,000<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Long Videos<\/td><td>\u20b950 \u2013 \u20b9200+<\/td><td>\u20b950,000 \u2013 \u20b92,00,000<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>So while Shorts help you grow quickly, long videos are what actually make you money.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How YouTube Splits the Ad Revenue?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>YouTube shares 55% of ad revenue with creators and keeps 45%.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>For example: <\/strong>If your CPM is \u20b9200,&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>YouTube keeps \u20b990 (45%)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>You earn \u20b9110 (55%)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>This split is standard worldwide and applies to both Indian and international creators.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Other Ways to Earn from YouTube (Besides Ads)?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Ads are just one part of YouTube income. Successful creators diversify their revenue using these methods:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Sponsorships<\/strong> \u2013 Collaborate with brands relevant to your niche.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Affiliate Marketing<\/strong> \u2013 Promote products using affiliate links.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Channel Memberships<\/strong> \u2013 Offer exclusive perks to loyal fans.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Super Chat &amp; Super Stickers<\/strong> \u2013 Earn during live streams.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Super Thanks<\/strong> \u2013 Fans pay to highlight their messages on your videos.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>YouTube Premium Revenue<\/strong> \u2013 Get a share when Premium users watch your content.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Selling Courses or Merchandise<\/strong> \u2013 Convert your audience into customers.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Must Read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-make-money-online-students\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Earn Money Online As a Student? 20 Ways<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Taxes on YouTube Income in India<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Yes, you must pay taxes on your YouTube income. Whether you earn from ads, sponsorships, or Shorts bonuses, it\u2019s all taxable under \u201cIncome from Other Sources.\u201d<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Indian creators need to link their PAN with AdSense.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>If you have international viewers, YouTube may deduct US tax before payment.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Keep records of your earnings and file ITR annually.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consult a CA if you earn regularly. It\u2019s worth staying compliant.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-e3e81fd07ffc59d8654e6a86732b30f9\"><strong>Read More Related Guides<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-digital-marketing\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What is Digital Marketing?<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/w